# D-93, the two-formal helper under --walk-methods: the walked call of a nested method carries one
# input (l2_mad_call), so this host stays native and l2trans notes it, located at the call; the
# native call builds the helper's node of its own arity.  add(1) = 9.  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: h2 (int: y; int: z) int
        return: n + y + z
    int: q (h2: 1 2)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: q + x
    return: addN

add: makeAdder 5
int: a (add: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 9
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
